  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Regional Copernicus Centre in Chile (CRC Chile)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;The project aims to establish a robust Copernicus Data Storage, Processing and Distribution Centre for the LAC region to be located in Santiago, Chile - with services including EO data processing, coordination of &lt;em&gt;in situ&lt;/em&gt; data of Chile and the LAC region &#xbf; search, publishing and regional EO services to be established in alliance with global Copernicus Services.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;This Copernicus Hub would take advantage of enhanced connectivity available between Europe and the LAC region by the on the BELLA Cable and the BELLA-T terrestrial fibre optic infrastructure, that allows fast and cost-effective data interchange between the two regions. It will develop from Chile&#xbf;s existing Hub and will provide resilience to the Copernicus services in the LAC region by working in team with the regional Copernicus centre - CopLAC Panama.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;It will deploy and install a highly reliable data storage and processing facility in Santiago with combined storage capacity in excess of 15 Petabytes of data and virtual machines servicing capacity of over 100 VMs (Virtual Machines) appropriately configured for EO data management and processing. This facility will also be synergic with Chile&#xbf;s High Performance Computing Laboratory. This facility will be capable of maintaining up to one year of online Sentinel data covering all the LAC region and to keep an archive of old data that will allow the recovery of past years series of Sentinel data. The facility will be connected to the REUNA/RedCLARA network at 100 Gbps to guarantee full access to the BELLA data transfer capabilities.&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
